---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleHero from '@/components/articles/ArticleHero.astro';
import ArticleContent from '@/components/articles/ArticleContent.astro';
import ArticleFAQ from '@/components/articles/ArticleFAQ.astro';
import StatsBar from '@/components/articles/StatsBar.astro';
import ArticleContactForm from '@/components/articles/ArticleContactForm.astro';
import ArticleTestimonials from '@/components/articles/ArticleTestimonials.astro';
import ArticleMap from '@/components/articles/ArticleMap.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "What should I do immediately after a bus accident?",
    answer: "Seek medical attention immediately, even if injuries seem minor. Document the scene with photos if possible, gather witness contact information, and report the accident to authorities. Contact an experienced bus accident attorney as soon as possible to preserve crucial evidence like video footage and maintenance records."
  },
  {
    question: "Who can be held liable in a bus accident case?",
    answer: "Liability in bus accidents can involve multiple parties including the bus driver, the bus company or transit authority (such as SMART or The Ride), maintenance contractors, or even manufacturers if a defect contributed to the accident. Our attorneys will thoroughly investigate to identify all responsible parties."
  },
  {
    question: "Can I file a claim if I was a passenger on the bus?",
    answer: "Yes, passengers injured in bus accidents have the right to pursue compensation. You may be eligible for claims through Michigan's no-fault insurance system and potentially against the at-fault party. Our firm will help you navigate both avenues to maximize your recovery."
  },
  {
    question: "How long do I have to file a bus accident claim in Michigan?",
    answer: "Michigan has strict deadlines for filing personal injury claims. Generally, you have three years from the date of the accident to file a lawsuit, but claims against government entities may have much shorter notice requirements. It's critical to contact an attorney immediately to ensure all deadlines are met."
  },
  {
    question: "What types of compensation can I recover after a bus accident?",
    answer: "Victims may be entitled to compensation for medical expenses, lost wages, pain and suffering, permanent disability, and in cases of wrongful death, funeral expenses and loss of companionship. Michigan's no-fault system also provides benefits for medical care and wage loss regardless of fault."
  },
  {
    question: "Do I need a lawyer if the bus company has offered me a settlement?",
    answer: "Yes, you should consult with an attorney before accepting any settlement offer. Bus companies and their insurers often make low initial offers that don't fully compensate victims for their injuries and losses. Our attorneys will evaluate whether the offer is fair and negotiate for the full compensation you deserve."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Bus Accident Lawyer Ann Arbor | Logeman & Iafrate, P.C."
  description="Experienced Ann Arbor bus accident attorneys helping victims of SMART, The Ride, and school bus accidents. Free consultation. Contingency-fee basis. Call (734) 994-0200."
  canonicalUrl="https://www.logeman.com/practice-area/bus-accidents/"
>
  <ArticleHero title="Bus Accident Lawyer Ann Arbor | Logeman & Iafrate, P.C." />

  <ArticleContent>
    <h2>Advocating For Bus Accident Victims In Ann Arbor</h2>
    <p>Navigating the aftermath of a bus accident can be exceptionally challenging. In Ann Arbor, where public and private buses are integral to daily transportation, the impact of these accidents can be far-reaching, affecting not only the victims but also their families and the community at large. At Logeman & Iafrate, P.C., we understand the complexities involved in bus accident cases. These accidents often involve multiple parties, severe injuries and complex negotiations.</p>

    <p>Whether you are a passenger, a pedestrian, or another driver involved in a bus accident, our experienced bus accident attorneys are here to offer the dedicated support and guidance you need. We recognize the physical, emotional and financial toll that a bus accident can impose. That's why we provide free consultations and represent our clients on a contingency-fee basis, ensuring that you can pursue justice without any upfront financial burden. Trust our experience and commitment as we strive to achieve the compensation and peace of mind you deserve.</p>

    <h2>Bus Accidents Can Have Deadly Consequences</h2>
    <p>Bus accidents encompass a range of incidents that can leave victims facing serious injuries and complex legal battles. Whether it's an incident involving a city bus, school bus or a service like SMART or The Ride, understanding your rights and the steps to take following an accident is crucial. At our Ann Arbor law firm, we can help guide you through these intricate cases and secure the compensation you deserve.</p>

    <p>Bus accidents can occur under various circumstances beyond collisions. These incidents may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Pedestrians being struck by a bus due to driver negligence or distracted driving.</li>
      <li>School children suffering injuries from inadequate supervision, bus driver errors, or unsafe boarding procedures.</li>
      <li>Passengers injured during boarding or exiting due to premature door closures, sudden stops, or unsafe stops.</li>
      <li>Individuals denied necessary accommodations or accessibility features leading to further harm.</li>
      <li>Slip and fall accidents on buses due to wet floors or debris.</li>
      <li>Collisions with other vehicles caused by bus driver error or mechanical failure.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Each scenario can lead to severe injuries such as traumatic brain injuries, spinal cord injuries, broken bones, soft tissue damage, and fatalities, leading to significant medical expenses and financial hardship for you and your family.</p>

    <h2>Why Legal Representation Is Critical For Bus Accident Claims</h2>
    <p>When dealing with bus accidents involving major transportation services like SMART, The Ride, or local school buses, you are often up against well-defended organizations. These entities have experienced legal teams dedicated to minimizing their liability. This reality makes it imperative to have knowledgeable and assertive legal representation on your side.</p>

    <p>Navigating the aftermath of a bus accident alone can be overwhelming. You may be eligible for claims through your auto <a href="/motor-vehicle-accidents-overview/no-fault-claim-attorney-ann-arbor-mi/">no-fault insurance</a>, but dealing with insurance companies can be challenging without legal expertise. When you work with us at Logeman & Iafrate, P.C., we will take the time to thoroughly investigate your case to determine the at-fault party. We know how to promptly obtain crucial evidence such as video footage, surveillance recordings, maintenance records, driver logs, and witness statements that are vital to your <a href="/motor-vehicle-accidents-overview/">personal injury case</a>.</p>

    <p>If you or someone you know has been involved in a bus accident, it is crucial to seek legal advice without delay. Quick action is necessary to preserve evidence, identify witnesses, and adhere to strict legal deadlines.</p>

    <h2>Speak With Our Experienced Bus Accident Attorneys Today</h2>
    <p>Whether you live in Ann Arbor, the Detroit metro area, or elsewhere in Michigan, our experienced bus accident lawyers are here to assist with your bus-related injury claims. Contact us anytime for advice and representation in achieving fair compensation for your injuries and losses. To schedule your free consultation, call us at (734) 228-4339 or fill out our <a href="/contact/">online contact form</a>. We take cases on a contingency-fee basis, so you never have to worry about upfront legal fees.</p>

    <h2>Our Story — Built on Experience and Determination</h2>
    <p>For decades, Logeman & Iafrate has represented injured clients across Michigan with unwavering commitment. We take cases others won't, and we win cases others can't. Our founders built this firm on a simple principle: injured people deserve fierce advocacy and real results.</p>

    <p class="text-[14px] text-muted-foreground italic mt-8">This article is provided for informational purposes only and does not constitute legal advice. Consult a qualified attorney at Logeman & Iafrate, P.C. for advice regarding your individual situation.</p>
  </ArticleContent>

  <ArticleFAQ items={faqs} />

  <StatsBar />

  <ArticleContactForm />

  <ArticleTestimonials />

  <ArticleMap />
</BaseLayout>
